<%--
Pdf_Viewer

Renders a PDF (the rendition url) via pdf.js onto a <canvas>, one page at a time. pdf.js is
lazy-loaded on first use from the framework streaming route (NOT in any bundle). The parent owns
pagination UI; this viewer only exposes set_page(n)/get_page()/get_pages() and emits events.

Arg: $url (the application/pdf source), $page (initial page, default 1), $fit (how the page is
scaled inside the box the host gave - "width" (default) or "contain"; anything else throws).

$fit="contain" requires a host with a BOUNDED HEIGHT to divide by; given none it falls back to the
width fit rather than rendering at a zero scale. The viewer re-renders the current page when that
box changes size (a debounced ResizeObserver), so growing the pane re-rasters instead of stretching
the old bitmap.
--%>
<Define:Pdf_Viewer tag="div">
    <canvas $sid="canvas" class="Pdf_Viewer__canvas"></canvas>
    <div $sid="error" class="Pdf_Viewer__error" style="display:none;">Unable to display this document.</div>
</Define:Pdf_Viewer>
